WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.172 --> 00:00:01.630
STEPHANIE WONG:
Today we're talking

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:05.320
about Gartner results, Cloud
Logging, Unattended Projects,

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.060
and Private Service Connect.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.730
I'm Stephanie Wong, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.070
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.620
For the fourth
consecutive year, Gartner

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.160
has positioned Google as a
leader in the 2021 Gartner

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.040
Magic Quadrant for Cloud
Infrastructure and Platform

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.240
Services.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.640
Our enterprise-ready
cloud provides you

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.010
the uptime,
performance, and scale

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.590
to run even your most
demanding workloads.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.600
And not to mention,
it saves you money

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.250
and has unmatched security.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.200
So check out the blog for more.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.960
To help you offload
operational tasks associated

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.840
with running your own logging
stack, we offer Cloud Logging.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.230
If you don't need to worry
about data residency,

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.910
Cloud Logging will
pick a region for you.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.360
But if you do have data
governance or compliance

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.540
requirements, we're excited to
share that Cloud Logging now

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.300
offers more flexibility and
control by providing you

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.220
a choice of 23 regions to store
and process your logging data.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.700
Things get busy, and it's not
uncommon to forget about one

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.600
of the many things
you've got going on,

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.630
including full projects.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.640
To help you prune your
idle Cloud resources,

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.370
we're excited to introduce
Unattended Project Recommender.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.750
It's a new ML-driven feature of
Active Assist that provides you

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.420
with a one-stop shop for
discovering, reclaiming,

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.730
and shutting down
unattended projects.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:28.670
Check it out in the
Recommender API today.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:30.830
Private Service
Correct is now in GA

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.680
and allows you to consume
services quickly, privately,

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.940
and securely.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.470
With Private
Service Connect, you

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.480
can create private
and secure connections

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.580
from your Cloud
networks to services

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.330
like Cloud Storage or Big
Table and third-party services

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.690
like Elastic,
MongoDB, or Snowflake.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.540
It creates service
endpoints in your VPCs

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:53.000
that provide private
connectivity and policy

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.100
enforcement, allowing
you to easily connect

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.317
services across different
networks and organizations.

00:01:59.317 --> 00:02:01.400
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.590
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.590
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:10.240
We'll see you in the Cloud.

